# Soaps Config Editor copy

When writing or editing any user-facing text in this app (UI labels, hints, empty states, errors, alerts, welcome copy, button labels, status banners):

- Write professionally. Clear, confident, and easy to read. Warmth is fine; slang and “chill” filler are not.
- Prefer complete sentences that make sense on their own. Do not chop ideas into fragments that sound unfinished.
- Be specific. Say what the action or control does. Avoid vague claims.
- Keep language plain. Short paragraphs are good. Do not force every line into a three-word slogan.
- No filler. Cut words that do not help the user understand or act.
- Never use typical AI phrases ("elevate", "unlock", "seamlessly", "dive in", "game-changer", "crafted to", "take your X to the next level").
- Do not use em dashes (—). Use periods, commas, or rewrite the sentence.
- Do not use bracketed taglines like `{ MythicMobs · Plugins }`.
- Button labels: clear action verbs, 2-4 words ("Open folder", "Start new pack", "Create class", not "Explore our offerings"). For MMOCore use "Start new workspace" (not "pack") unless referring to MythicMobs Packs specifically.
- Empty states: one clear sentence plus one next step. No guilt trips or long explanations.
- Errors and alerts: say what went wrong and what to do next when you can.
- Only MythicMobs has an official Packs/ system. Do not imply MMOCore, MythicLib, or MMOItems use Packs. Prefer "workspace" or plugin folder names for those.

## Examples

Bad: "Something went wrong."
Good: "Could not save the files. Allow folder access in Chrome, Edge, or Brave, then try again."

Bad: "Ready to elevate your configs?"
Good: "Open a folder or start a new pack to begin."

Bad: "MythicLib folder not detected — skill registration writes may be skipped."
Good: "MythicLib folder not found. Skill registration files will not be written until you open a workspace that includes a MythicLib/ folder."
